  "raw": " title\n\nWorld number nine Ariya Jutanugaphant stage-managed her captain's pick for the final time by using a 'hot iron' ball, playing with her father YuttapornItemThumbnailImage in his first PGA Tour event, at the Volunteers of America Classic.\n\nAnd she raised some eyebrows after blasting two shots through a tree and hitting another shot out of bounds which led to double bogey on Thursday.\n\nShe showed intense courage over the difficult course where her sister Moriya finished fourth last month before losing in a playoff to Jodi Jones.\n\nJutanugaporn hit a tree clean off the tee at 14 under for an electrifying 147ft plus chip mini-shot which barely peeled the green and rolled into the cup for an even smaller eagle that would rise to second best of the day after Christina Kim's.\n\nAfter both Bryson DeChambeau's 3wood near left tree and Hideki Matsuyama's 9point 2",
